There are lots of examples where LaTeX's algorithm works. That is why
Lamport released it: it works often enough to be useful! There are lots
of examples where it doesn't work as expected [but it does work as
documented in the LaTeX manual and in latex.tex!].

In 7 years of sporadic updates of the univ of utah thesis LaTeX style
sources many significant examples have appeared. A recent example:
Tang's PhD thesis, 300 pages of LaTeX with over 100 figures and tables.
Nelson Beebe spent over 100 hours helping Tang with the figures. A
significant trouble for Tang was figure placement and the float
algorithm (maybe it still is, he is supposed to submit a final copy in
December).

Communication of the actual problem with floats seems to be a
difficulty. There are some simple test files (<200 lines) that can
illustrate the problems better than I can do in words. If you are really
interested, Mike, then I'll email an example to you personally.

